Q: Text centered next to the image header A: <p>You can do this pretty easily using a float left, which is one of the oldest methods to make the image display on the left</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.header-container &gt; img {
 float: left;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;header class="site-header"&gt;
  &lt;div class="header-container m-4"&gt;
    &lt;img src="https://placehold.co/200x140" alt="Logo" width="140" height="200" class="header-logo"&gt;
    &lt;h1&gt;Capitol 52 Foundation&lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;P.O. Box 75421 Vienna, VA 23236&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;</code></pre>
